## v0.20 AI super overhaul (next)
AI work goes under v0.20, then v0.20.1, v0.20.2 and so on.
- Bug to look at first: an AI task force that starts far away shows Attack_Unit in the F3 developer view but sails in circles instead of closing (seen 13 Oct, Shokaku group at about 14-16 km).
- **v0.20** Stuck attackers `[AIMOVE]` (ai_super_overhaul.md): far-off AI task forces circling a waypoint instead of closing now steer straight at their target, with a land check (tested)
- **Surface tactics:** close to the right range for their guns, try to cross your T, keep destroyers and light cruisers out of heavy-gun range until their torpedo run, pull damaged ships out of the line.
- **Carrier groups:** carriers keep away from your surface ships, launch strikes and CAP on their own, escorts screen the carriers.
  - Carriers can't launch or recover aircraft in battle (vanilla). Idea: aircraft that reach their carrier "land" (disappear) and, after a rearm time, a fresh flight is launched from the carrier. No new assets needed (the game's aircraft models are reused, there just wouldn't be a landing animation). The game builds aircraft groups only at battle start (`EngagementData.CreateUnitGroup`), so this needs checking first: if that method can be called again mid-battle, it's doable. Both sides, needs an intact flight deck.
- **Strategic AI (campaign):** planned operations (invasions, convoys, bombardments with cover), reacting to your fleet movements.
- **v0.20.1 Anti-air manoeuvres `[AAEVADE]` (aa_evade.md, tested; v0.20.2 fixes tested: unstick, formations turn together, earlier warning, comb torpedo tracks, rudder reversal):** player and AI ships turn and evade during air attacks *before* bombs drop or torpedoes are in the water. Torpedo bombers on their run make the ship turn to point her bow or stern at them (the smallest target). Dive bombers starting their dive make her go to full speed with the rudder hard over. Afterwards she goes back to her course or formation.
  - Checked in the game code: possible, and the game has nothing like it now. The "hazard evasion" toggle (`UnitAI.noNavEvade`, used in `UnitAISea.CheckNavigation`) only stops ships colliding with each other. Torpedoes spotted in the water are only put on the map (`SensorManager.CheckAiTorpedoDetection`). So no ship turns away from aircraft or torpedoes, which is why they "brute force" the attacks.
  - Plan: a new check about every second looks through `EngagementManager.allAirUnits` for enemy aircraft that have this ship as their target and are on their attack run inside about 3 km. It then sets the ship's speed and rudder (`wantedSpeed` / `wantedTurnRate`) for a short evasive turn. Player ships follow the existing evasion toggle, so you can switch it off. Ships in formation break off and rejoin afterwards. A follow-up could also turn ships to comb torpedoes already seen in the water. Tag `[AAEVADE]`.
- **v0.20.3 Realistic air attack heights and bomb aim `[BOMBAIM]` (air_realism.md, tested 14 Oct: 69 US 1942 dive bomber bombs, 11 hits or near misses, typical miss 70 m):** found in the code: only dive bombers get a set start height (2,000-2,200 m, our v0.17 change, `EngagementData.CreateUnitGroup`); every other aircraft is capped at 3,300 m there. Bombs have no aim scatter, and the dive bomber's aim allows for the ship's speed *and* turn (`UnitAIAir.InterceptTarget`), so drops are near perfect.
  - Start heights by type, from history: dive bombers about 4,000-5,000 m (push over about 1,200 m out, release 450-600 m), torpedo bombers 300-600 m (drop at 30-60 m), level bombers 4,000-6,000 m (Betty), B-17 6,000-7,500 m. The 3,300 m cap goes up to match.
  - Aim error at release, larger when the ship is turning hard and under heavy flak, and set by crew quality for the nation and year (US 1942 dive bombing hit roughly 10-25% against a ship at full speed; the elite Japanese crews of early 1942 did much better). High level bombing against ships at sea should hit very rarely, as it did.
- **v0.20.4 Fighter manoeuvres `[DOGFIGHT]` (dogfight.md, tested 14 Oct: boom and zoom and slashing passes work; all 24 escorts piled onto one Zero, fixed in v0.20.6):** dogfights look like planes on rails. Planes in this game only steer, change height and change speed, so real fighter moves can be built from those: break turns when someone gets on your tail (the game already has Break_Left / Break_Right), turn fights, scissors, high yo-yo, boom and zoom (dive, shoot, climb away), and the Thach Weave for US pairs. Following history: Zeros want to turn-fight, Wildcats dive in, keep their speed and don't turn with Zeros. True barrel rolls depend on how the models bank, so they may be limited to the flight path.
- **v0.20.5 Torpedo bomber runs `[TORPRUN]` (torpedo_runs.md, tested):** no drops closer than 600 m; flights astern of their target fly round to get ahead first, and only attack from astern after 2 minutes.
- **v0.20.6 Fixes (fixes_v0.20.6.md, tested):** fighters pick their target again between passes so they spread out; only one of two stuck ships gives way, then both turn apart.
- **v0.20.7 Fixes (fixes_v0.20.7.md, tested: runs last ~8 s, 3 Zeros shot down for no Wildcats):** Wildcat gun runs no longer end the moment they start (they were zoom climbing forever), zoom climbs capped at 1 km above the target, torpedo drop check only on the run in.
- **v0.20.8 Fighter rules `[FIGHTRULE]` (fighter_rules.md, tested: spreading works):** fighters fight aircraft before strafing ships; at most 4 fighters on one enemy plane.
- **v0.20.9 Fixes (fixes_v0.20.9.md, FAILED test, aircraft work on hold):** our own aimed gun run (nose pointed up and down at the lead point, up to 45 degree aiming dives), passes end after flying past the target instead of after 8 s; formations keep combing torpedo tracks with their leader.
- **v0.20.10 Fighter manoeuvres you can see (planned):** checked in the code: the bank is worked out in `UnitAir.ApplyFlightControls` (roll = turn rate x -5, smoothed) and applied with the pitch and heading in `UnitAir.ApplyUnitMovement`. The game already overrides it for the dive bombers' roll-over (`PerformManeuvre`, `Library.rollOver`), so the same can be done for fighters. Planes move straight along their nose, so rolling is safe to show; anything that pitches the nose (loops, split-S) also changes the flight path and needs care.
  - Deeper banks in hard turns, and roll speed by plane (the Zero slow to roll at high speed).
  - Aileron rolls and jinks when breaking away from an attacker, a wing-over at the top of a zoom climb, a half roll into the dive for a split-S.
- **Submarines and ASW:** smarter sub attacks, better enemy destroyer hunting of your subs.
